# Mutation testing artefacts (mutmut copies the tree into ./mutants)
mutants/
.mutmut-cache

# Local working documents — planning notes, task and fix lists, the reports an
# agent session leaves behind, and local instructions for Claude Code. None of
# these are project code and none belong in a public repo: a *_FIXES.md is a
# map of what is not fixed yet.
#
# They were only ever protected by .git/info/exclude, which lives inside .git
# and travels with no clone — so on any second machine there was nothing
# stopping them being committed.
#
# `oiueei_*.md` covers the product, deployment, legal and glossary notes that
# live in the author's own documents folder and get copied in here to be worked
# on. Unlike the files above, they arrive by a plain `cp`, so nothing about them
# looks temporary to a `git add -A` run three commits later.
*_TASKS.md
*_FIXES.md
LEGAL_HEROKU.md
oiueei_*.md
CLAUDE.local.md
*_REPORT.md
*_REVIEW_*.md
